WEBVTT

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:18.600
Mother...

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:21.270
Goodbye.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.310
Goodbye, my "curse."

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:36.030
It's your fault!

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:39.370
--Irredeemable!
--We know your sins!

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:40.790
What are you doing there?

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:49.540
You're...

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:55.010
I know you'll accept me.

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:57.090
You don't know anything.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:01.720
And you're alone.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:06.100
Richard, forgive me.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:11.070
These aren't my memories, I'm certain.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:14.320
They're fragments I've heard

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:18.410
from the tale of another Henry
who looked so much like me.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:29.500
Where is the enemy now?

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:34.010
Reports place them in
the vicinity of Tamworth.

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:37.180
We'll fight on Bosworth field, then.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:39.050
Inform the men.

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:42.810
There will be no food
or rest on the battlefield.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:45.430
Let them enjoy their last suppers tonight.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.310
He's so haggard.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:53.940
Why does God demand so much of him?

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.490
You too, Catesby.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:00.200
If you want something, name it.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:05.700
No fine wine or gift could
fully repay your loyalty.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.790
I wish only for Your Majesty's
health and peace of mind.

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:10.710
Speak your true desire!

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:13.920
Don't wish for my sake!

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:17.050
What would you do if I was gone?

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:20.590
What would you live for if
all this was no more?

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:49.710
I believed that only my
crown remained to me.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:52.420
And yet...

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:54.130
Your father

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:57.800
was not Richard Plantagenet, Duke of York.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:01.300
Did he know?

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.810
Did Father know all along?

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:23.160
If even my name and my blood
were all an illusion,

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:26.990
then what is the sense of this war?

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:41.470
Hey, where are you going?

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:46.850
Strange.

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:50.430
Something like this

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:51.890
happened before.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:03.450
It's warm.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:09.490
Far warmer than that empty bed.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:15.500
I might as well just...

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:19.800
You think so too?

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:24.260
It feels good to sleep here.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.050
It...

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:30.310
It can't be.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:31.430
You're...

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:42.940
Have you come to kill me, James Tyrrell?!

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:45.530
That isn't my real name.

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:48.530
I have no name now.

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:51.830
No name, no past, no friends.

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:54.710
Nothing.

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:59.170
Nothing.

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:05.050
Even Buckingham is gone now.
He has no more need to kill me.

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:08.890
I truly have nothing left.

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:14.270
I believed that claiming the crown
would gain me paradise,

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:19.270
but that paradise was
home to myself alone.

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:21.940
I didn't mind that.

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:25.990
Solitude had been kind to me.

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:28.240
But now, I find it...

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:29.570
Richard,

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:33.450
if you want to flee,
I'll take you from here.

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:37.960
If you wish for salvation...

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.880
After all, you have nothing left.

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:44.960
Henry,

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:50.050
were you also afflicted by isolation
within your royal crown?

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:53.720
I've never wished to
see you more strongly.

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:58.100
The weight of the crown.
The coldness of the royal bed.

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:02.150
I have so many things
to talk with you about now.

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:05.650
But that day, at the end,

00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:09.490
why were you on the battlefield?

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:13.990
You must have had the means to escape.

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:23.550
That rainy night you spent
with the Duke of Buckingham,

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:28.590
I learned what this emptiness
truly is for the first time.

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:31.090
I'm not here merely to perish.

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:35.720
To sustain my existence,
I want just one...

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:36.930
One ray of light.

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:38.020
Impossible.

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:40.190
To him, the crown was--

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:42.480
Light is not paradise.

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:44.570
You ought to know that too.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:47.820
Light and briars are one and the same.

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:51.320
Even so,

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:53.200
you can't help seeking it.

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:01.880
Because to seek is the meaning of living.

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:03.630
Whitey, wait.

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:06.340
That isn't the way home.

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:09.220
Will you go with that boar?

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:13.350
I doubt it can survive long in the forest.

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:25.480
Yes, you'll go home.

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:29.780
You don't care if the world rejects you,

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:32.410
as long as that's where you want to be.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:39.410
What will you do?

00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:42.330
Where do you long to be?

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:43.790
I...

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:45.380
I wish to be...

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:51.800
...neither beneath a cold
canopy nor in a warm forest.

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:58.100
I gained everything and
became king with this body.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:00.850
Not by blood or by name.

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:02.440
I wished for it.

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:08.110
<i>That </i>is my reason to fight.

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:16.370
Then, you'll return to the battlefield.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:18.120
It's where the king belongs.

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:23.160
I have a request for you.

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:29.840
Would you be my light?

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:31.970
Your light?

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:37.180
We've both lost so many things.

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:46.400
I want you... to be my friend.

00:08:57.030 --> 00:09:00.290
Yes, let's be friends.

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:04.080
Thank you, Richard.

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:14.420
Now, let us return.

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:20.810
Even if a sleepless battlefield awaits me.

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:29.810
As long as that's the place I sought.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:34.690
You're my friend.

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:41.950
Now, I can have no regrets...

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:46.870
...when I kill you,

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:48.120
Richard.

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:57.680
York of the white rose.

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:00.220
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:06.730
These royal houses with roses for
their crests battled for the throne.

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:11.610
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:20.370
The world's in an uproar again.

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:22.280
Our livelihood's up and vanished.

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:25.500
Shall we look for the next James Tyrrell?

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:28.120
Forrest, Dighton,

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:32.880
I'll send you some news
as thanks for feeding me.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:38.630
How many times have I
returned to war since childhood?

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:43.350
At first, I merely sought revenge.
And now...

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:46.520
Archers, front and center.

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:48.180
Howard, take command.

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:51.770
Stanley, Northumberland,
see to your own troops.

00:10:51.770 --> 00:10:53.690
--At once!
--Certainly.

00:10:55.650 --> 00:10:58.070
Where is Stanley?

00:10:58.070 --> 00:11:01.910
Observing Richmond's army,
or so he claims.

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:04.870
Tell him to array his troops
by dawn tomorrow.

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:11.210
It appears my stepfather
still can't make up his mind.

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:13.790
Is this the time to be so easygoing?

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:16.500
I hear that the foe outnumbers us.

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:20.430
And most of those extra troops
are under my stepfather's command.

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:24.260
And what if that wasn't all?
What if most of our foes

00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:26.930
sided with us?

00:11:29.310 --> 00:11:30.600
Your Majesty!

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:32.770
Don't worry. It's nothing.

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:39.820
Lord Northumberland,

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:41.700
has it reached you too?

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:46.700
This letter was apparently sent to
the major leaders of the king's army.

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:52.290
Henry Tudor, Earl of Richmond,

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:57.380
has formally married Elizabeth,
daughter of Edward IV.

00:11:57.380 --> 00:11:59.380
These signatures are genuine.

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:04.510
In which case, Richmond is no longer
a mere Lancastrian usurper.

00:12:05.470 --> 00:12:10.520
He will be a righteous hero,
shouldering the regrets of kings past.

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:23.030
Howard, thank you for your report.

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:25.870
The cowards only know underhanded tricks.

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:29.080
Tomorrow, we'll teach them
how to fight with swords.

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:35.210
Your Majesty.

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:38.920
Unsettling rumors were already
circulating before our march.

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:44.050
Your Majesty, please retreat.

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:46.470
Even if your throne is taken now,

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:51.520
you reclaim it once you rally
and regain your strength.

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:58.820
I won't get another chance.
This deadly illness worsens by the day.

00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:05.450
I thought I was leaving my peaceful
palace for a bloody, dreadful battlefield.

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:10.040
But now that I'm here,
my heart is shockingly calm.

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:15.580
I'm certain now:
this is where the king belongs.

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:17.790
This is the place I sought.

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:22.630
Do you plan to die in battle?

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:31.970
You told me to name my desire.

00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:34.350
I...

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:41.940
I only wished that you could
walk the path you desired.

00:13:43.490 --> 00:13:50.160
Never once have I barred your way
for the sake of my own desires.

00:13:51.490 --> 00:13:55.290
But if you'll hear one
selfish request at the end,

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:57.420
then please...

00:13:57.420 --> 00:13:59.500
Please grant my wish.

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:05.220
King Richard, live!

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:06.880
Live for me!

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:22.770
Forgive me, Catesby.

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:35.000
Forgive me.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.620
I'm frightened!

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:39.290
I dreamed of a horrible forest!

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:48.800
Please, have no more nightmares.

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:51.510
Never again.

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:08.070
My lord!

00:15:08.070 --> 00:15:09.150
Yes?

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:12.030
Someone claims to have information for us.

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:20.500
Tell me.

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:24.590
How did you feel about this body of mine?

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:29.340
I've found you beautiful.

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:32.050
Ever since you were born.

00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:41.310
I am the king.

00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:43.690
I will not fight to lose.

00:15:52.410 --> 00:15:57.580
Gentlemen! Richard III is a
bloody tyrant and a homicide!

00:15:57.580 --> 00:16:01.120
One raised in blood,
and one in blood established!

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:06.250
He schemed to come by what he has and
slaughtered even his fellow schemers!

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:09.090
Since the moment of his birth,

00:16:09.090 --> 00:16:12.680
that demon has ever been God's enemy!

00:16:16.010 --> 00:16:17.850
Draw your swords now!

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:21.890
Bend your bows like full moons!
Spur your chargers into a sea of blood!

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:26.520
A crown...

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:28.190
...or an honorable death!

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:50.210
Your Majesty, our front line is faltering!

00:16:50.210 --> 00:16:54.550
We still have Lords Stanley and
Northumberland's forces in reserve!

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:58.600
The enemy knows that too.

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:03.600
Oxford is a proven veteran.
Why would he waste his men like this?

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:07.440
Order Northumberland to advance.

00:17:11.780 --> 00:17:16.450
I cannot join in a war without a future.

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:19.740
How could the Earl of
Northumberland betray us?

00:17:19.740 --> 00:17:23.250
More traitors are sure to follow.

00:17:23.250 --> 00:17:27.500
To think that I still had more to lose.

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:33.210
I can't blame them. Who would
choose to join a demon's fall to hell?

00:17:33.210 --> 00:17:34.380
In which case...

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:37.800
I will go!

00:17:53.610 --> 00:17:54.570
Your Majesty!

00:17:55.860 --> 00:17:57.950
Fight! Don't give an inch!

00:17:57.950 --> 00:18:00.120
Your king is here!

00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:03.540
That's...

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:05.210
Richmond's main line!

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:07.330
Stanley's forces lie ahead!

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:09.330
If he went for reinforcements...

00:18:13.550 --> 00:18:16.930
Those who would enter heaven, leave us.

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:20.550
But if you would follow me,

00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:22.470
we go to hell together!

00:18:25.980 --> 00:18:28.270
Follow the king!

00:18:37.530 --> 00:18:39.570
Richmond!

00:18:56.010 --> 00:18:57.590
A body double?!

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:04.260
A king hardly needs to fight personally.

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:06.890
Call me when the battle is over.

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:14.400
All troops, advance.

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:16.150
Our enemy is...

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:23.240
...the vile King Richard III!

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:27.450
My fate is sealed.

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:32.830
But...

00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:41.890
I care not how loudly the world wails,

00:19:41.890 --> 00:19:43.850
nor how firmly God denies me.

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:48.350
Again, and again...

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:52.350
...and again...

00:19:54.110 --> 00:19:57.110
...I will reach for the light.

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:03.280
Won't someone come for me?

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:05.620
Everyone went away.

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:13.210
Richard, I'm right here.

00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:21.800
I was always alone.

00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:25.680
I am neither a man nor a woman.

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:30.180
I thought of myself as
the loathsome Joan of Arc.

00:20:32.770 --> 00:20:36.020
That's right. You were me.

00:20:37.070 --> 00:20:40.990
Me bound by my curse,
convinced that even to wish was a sin.

00:20:42.150 --> 00:20:45.870
You feared demons,
sought solace in your wounds,

00:20:45.870 --> 00:20:49.040
and despised yourself more than anyone.

00:20:50.370 --> 00:20:54.000
The other me from back then.

00:20:57.670 --> 00:21:01.800
Now, is it time for my cue?

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:07.220
If your information proves true,
I'll give you the title you desire,

00:21:07.220 --> 00:21:08.810
my dear Tyrrell.

00:21:10.350 --> 00:21:12.430
Did you slay Richard?

00:21:12.430 --> 00:21:15.810
Well... He fell from his horse.
After that, I don't know.

00:21:15.810 --> 00:21:18.150
And was his horse black?

00:21:18.150 --> 00:21:19.770
Yes, sir. I think so.

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:23.740
That was a fake.

00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:25.860
The real Richard is mounted...

00:21:30.040 --> 00:21:32.040
...on a white steed.

00:21:41.050 --> 00:21:43.840
Who are you?

00:21:45.510 --> 00:21:47.180
I am you.

00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:51.850
I love you,

00:21:51.850 --> 00:21:53.100
Richard.

00:21:59.520 --> 00:22:01.820
Richard.

00:22:01.820 --> 00:22:03.280
Richard.

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:17.620
Richard, I...

00:22:19.630 --> 00:22:23.250
I love you.

00:22:26.300 --> 00:22:30.300
Fate turns and turns again.

00:22:33.430 --> 00:22:36.430
No matter how many times I seize it...

00:22:40.860 --> 00:22:43.980
No matter how many times I lose it...

00:22:46.530 --> 00:22:49.450
I refuse to let you die!

00:22:49.450 --> 00:22:52.200
Not even if you wish for it!

00:23:00.710 --> 00:23:02.500
Very well.

00:23:02.500 --> 00:23:04.210
When I wake,

00:23:05.590 --> 00:23:07.550
I'll grant your wish.

00:23:28.700 --> 00:23:30.160
But now...

00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:34.990
Now, for just a short while,

00:23:36.790 --> 00:23:38.910
let me sleep

00:23:40.080 --> 00:23:41.790
in a beautiful dream.
